1
00:00:00,460 --> 00:00:05,800
Why does AI sometimes answer confidently,
and get it wrong?

2
00:00:05,830 --> 00:00:11,420
Researchers at OpenAI say a big reason is
how we grade it.

3
00:00:11,450 --> 00:00:15,250
On a multiple-choice exam, a guess might
score.

4
00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:18,030
A blank always scores zero.

5
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:21,350
So guessing beats "I don't know."

6
00:00:21,380 --> 00:00:25,450
In one test, a model that held back on
about half the questions

7
00:00:25,450 --> 00:00:28,310
was wrong 26 percent of the time.

8
00:00:28,340 --> 00:00:32,230
One that rarely held back got slightly
more right,

9
00:00:32,230 --> 00:00:36,940
but was wrong 75 percent.

10
00:00:36,970 --> 00:00:41,210
A guess has a one in 365 chance.

11
00:00:41,240 --> 00:00:44,350
"I don't know" scores zero.

12
00:00:44,380 --> 00:00:48,670
Their fix: penalise confident errors more
than uncertainty,

13
00:00:48,670 --> 00:00:52,520
and reward an honest "I don't know."

14
00:00:52,550 --> 00:00:57,580
So, for facts that matter, ask for the
source, and check it.

